.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Visual debugging aids\&. 

Internal header\&.
.PP
Invalidation bugs are invisible by construction: too little marking leaves stale pixels that look plausible, and too much marking looks perfectly correct while quietly repainting the whole window every frame\&. Neither shows up in a screenshot\&. Tinting the region that is actually being repainted makes both failures obvious at a glance, which is why the roadmap asks for this before the third widget exists rather than after the first bug report\&.
.PP
\fBNot part of the host facing interface\&.\fP A development aid\&. A host binds to \fBschultz_api\&.h\fP; this header is the toolkit's own and may change without notice\&. 
.PP
Definition in file \fBschultz_debug\&.h\fP\&.
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "int32_t schultz_debug_tint_dirty (\fBschultz_draw_list\fP * list, const \fBschultz_tree\fP * tree, \fBschultz_color\fP color)"

.PP
Appends a tinted overlay marking the tree's dirty region\&. Draws a translucent fill plus a solid outline over the area that will be repainted this frame\&. Call it last, after the scene, so the tint sits on top of what it describes\&.
.PP
Nothing is appended when the tree is clean\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIlist\fP The draw list to append to\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fItree\fP The tree whose dirty region should be shown\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIcolor\fP The tint\&. Its alpha is used for the fill; the outline is drawn at full opacity so a very thin region is still visible\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT when either pointer is NULL, or an append error\&. 
.RE
.PP

